harness/render.py:3:The single most important thing here: the voice and the text are NOT two systems.
harness/render.py:4:They read the same event stream at different verbosity. Anything the voice says is
harness/render.py:5:something you could have read; anything you can read, the voice can summarize.
harness/render.py:7:    VOICE  →  a sentence. Spoken-length. "Riggs is on it — two minutes."
harness/render.py:10:The voice can ESCALATE into the text stream on request ("what's it actually doing?").
harness/render.py:14:Why voice must stay short (this is not a style preference):
harness/render.py:16:content as text. A chatty voice is an expensive voice. Short spoken summaries with
harness/render.py:28:    "dispatched": "started",
harness/render.py:42:    "dispatched": "→", "thinking": "·", "read": "◇", "edit": "✎", "write": "+",
harness/render.py:51:    'Riggs' alone doesn't tell you whether your auth module was built by your best
harness/render.py:76:        f"  branch: {job['branch'] or '—'}",
harness/render.py:105:# VOICE — a colleague, not a log reader.
harness/render.py:109:#      I'll report back when he's done, and review is happening.'"
harness/render.py:111:# So the voice NEVER speaks in tool calls. No "read", no "edit", no "bash", no file
harness/render.py:114:# The voice speaks in three things a person would actually say:
harness/render.py:120:# colleague says and "read auth.py, then edited routes.py" is what a log says.
harness/render.py:127:# Editing dispatch.py, writing test_ratelimit.py. I don't know what that means…
harness/render.py:130:# So the voice NEVER emits:
harness/render.py:131:#   - a filename or path    (dispatch.py, backend/app/routes.py)
harness/render.py:143:    "dispatched": "just getting started",
harness/render.py:163:def announce_dispatch(lane: str, task_name: str, reviewers: int = 0) -> str:
harness/render.py:167:    commitment, what's next — one breath. The model is NOT named here: at dispatch
