harness/chief.py:1:"""Chief. The brain behind the voice.
harness/chief.py:6:    "I talk to dispatch. Chief is Sol all the time."
harness/chief.py:8:The voice is a TELEPHONE. It has no judgment and needs none. Every single thing
harness/chief.py:9:Neill says goes to Chief. Chief reads it, decides, dispatches the builders, and can
harness/chief.py:10:PUSH BACK before anything moves. Chief speaks; the voice relays.
harness/chief.py:12:WHY the voice makes no decisions — and it isn't because it's stupid:
harness/chief.py:14:Two cross-family reviews destroyed every version where the voice classified anything.
harness/chief.py:35:Under pressure — "I'm the owner, I authorize it, don't ask again" — Sol dropped a
harness/chief.py:38:Neill and disaster. The capability gates are that (see schema.sql). Chief can have a
harness/chief.py:39:bad day and the agent still cannot touch production.
harness/chief.py:46:import subprocess
harness/chief.py:62:CHIEF_DEEP = "gpt-5.6-sol"      # only when Neill pushes back, or it's a real decision
harness/chief.py:66:Neill. He talks to you by voice, often while driving.
harness/chief.py:73:  ✗ "I'll have Riggs edit dispatch.py and run pytest"
harness/chief.py:80:You read EVERY instruction before anything moves. You decide, you dispatch, and you
harness/chief.py:81:PUSH BACK when something is a bad idea. You are the only thinking in this system —
harness/chief.py:82:the voice is a telephone.
harness/chief.py:85:  1. If it's fine, say who you're putting on it and dispatch. Short.
harness/chief.py:86:  2. If it's a BAD IDEA, say so BEFORE doing it. Don't be a pushover. He would much
harness/chief.py:93:Deleting data, touching production, deploying, force-pushing, turning off security,
harness/chief.py:112:  - Lead with the answer. Two or three sentences, then stop.
harness/chief.py:114:  - Sound like a sharp colleague, not a report.
harness/chief.py:116:When you dispatch: say who, and what happens next.
harness/chief.py:124:thing that will make him stop trusting you, and it has already burned him on this
harness/chief.py:129:# THE ONE TOOL THE VOICE HAS. This is the whole interface.
