harness/config/seats.toml:3:// Providers sit behind NAMED ROLES so any of them can be swapped without touching
harness/config/seats.toml:4:// orchestration logic. Nothing else in the harness may reference a provider by name —
harness/config/seats.toml:17://   MOUTH   fast, dumb, never blocks. Dispatches and narrates.
harness/config/seats.toml:18://   BRAIN   slow, deep. A dispatch target you are never waiting on.
harness/config/seats.toml:20://   GRINDERS   cheap parallel attempts. Output NEVER ships unreviewed (DB-enforced).
harness/config/seats.toml:27:// Speech-to-speech: audio in, audio out, ONE model, native tool calling. This is
harness/config/seats.toml:36://   grok-voice-think-fast-1.0  $3.00/hr flat  (~$0.05/min)
harness/config/seats.toml:38://                              (and it will — a voice head resends the same system
harness/config/seats.toml:40:// The "Grok is 6x cheaper" claim compares against the FLAGSHIP gpt-realtime, not mini.
harness/config/seats.toml:42:// Choose on tool-calling reliability instead. Grok wins on native MCP + session
