codex
The most important scope leak is now concrete: “voice can never open a door” is only true if a repository merge has no automatic real-world effect. The design does not yet require proof of that before a repository is admitted. A spoken request can become an automatic merge; if that repository publishes a site, deploys on merge, updates live configuration, or runs privileged automation, voice has indirectly reached production. That is a design gap, not a demand for enterprise release machinery.
